# Core, notifiers and CLI

- `crc/core` policy and age code is pure: plain data in, decision out, no I/O, and time only
  through the injected `now` (existing exception: `is_old` reads `MAX_AGE`; add no new env read).
  Fail closed on unparseable input.
- Notifiers consume the `Report` only and hold no cloud logic.
- New env reads, prints and exits go in `crc/cli` (other layers: ARCH-003); it parses and
  validates flag values before any cloud call.
- A CLI flag is an external contract (Jenkins jobs in `cloud-resource-cleanup-triggers`): never
  rename, remove, re-type or change a default; a new flag is optional. See the flag workflow in
  `AGENTS.md`.
- New kinds run on the engine path (`crc/cli/routes/`), not as new legacy handlers.
- Run-log text follows `docs/logging.md`.
